drm/rockchip: ebc: four correctness fixes in the direct-mode driver

From a third-party source review of the tree at generation 9
(doc/reviews/2026-09-03-third-party-audit.md), with the EXTRACT_FBS
hunks re-done after the 2026-09-04 adversarial review caught a dangling
else in the first version (a successful extraction returned -EFAULT and
a bad pointer returned 0; the build log carried five -Wdangling-else
warnings that were not read).

1. The parallel advance ran a band inline when queue_work() returned
   false.  False means the work is already queued and that invocation
   owns the completion; running it inline would process the band twice
   and complete() twice.  A fresh on-stack item never returns false;
   WARN_ON_ONCE() it and wait like everyone else.
2. The 32x32 dither path loaded both 16-byte halves of a texture row
   from the same address, so the blue-noise pattern repeated its first
   half.  The second load starts 16 bytes in.  Three copies, one per
   pixel format.
3. rect_hint_batch is snapshotted once per ioctl and validated
   (1..4096; zero spun the copy loop forever), and the rectangle count
   is capped at 65536 (-E2BIG).
4. OFF_SCREEN returned the uncopied byte count; EXTRACT_FBS ORed copy
   residuals and errnos together.  Both now return -EFAULT on any
   short copy, with every branch braced.

